:answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}+1}(x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309794} :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311504}] :question/math-academy-id "q-337707" :question/problem "Suppose we would like to find an integrating factor to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}{y}^{′}=-x{y}^{3}-x,\\,x>0\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation using an integrating factor. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(y)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{y}.$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in differential form. This gives\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=x({y}^{3}+1),\\,Q(x,y)={y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\,{{field-4}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\,{{field-5}}\n$$\n\nSince for this equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})={{field-6}},\n$$\n\nwhich depends on $y$ only, then an integrating factor for our equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-7}},\n$$\n\nand we arrive at the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-8}}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Integrating Factor for an Inexact Equation: Condition on Y Satisfied" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049187 :topic/math-academy-id 6353 :topic/title "Solving Exact ODEs Using Integrating Factors"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186217250 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186217792 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216598} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216599} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216600} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216601}] :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216597} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{2}y^{4} + 3x^{2}y^{2} + xy = c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216603} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4}y^{3} + 2x^{3}y^{2} + y = c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216604} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}y^{3} + 2xy^{2} + y = c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216605} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}y^{2} + xy^{2} + xy = c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216606}] :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216602} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}{y}^{4}+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+xy=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391639} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}{y}^{3}+2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}+y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391640} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x{y}^{2}+xy=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391641} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}{y}^{3}+2x{y}^{2}+y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}{y}^{3}+2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}+y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391640} :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391638} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391644} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391645} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391646} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391645} :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391643}] :question/math-academy-id "q-337096" :question/problem "Consider the inexact differential equation\n\n$$\n(\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{x}+4{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+(4y+3x{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\nIt is known that \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=\\frac{3}{x}\n$$\n\nwhere the functions $P$ and $Q$ are given by \n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{x}+4{y}^{3},\\,Q(x,y)=4y+3x{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nUse this information to find a suitable integrating factor $I(x)$ and hence find the general solution to the equation.\n\n$\\,$ A suitable integrating factor is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is {{field-2}}, where $c$ is a constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186217793 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216608} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216609} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216610} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216611}] :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216607} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{4}}{y^{4}} - 2y = c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216613} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{3}}{y^{3}} - 2y = c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216614} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{y^{2}} - 2y^{2} = c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216615} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{4}}{y^{4}} - 2y^{3} = c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216616}] :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216612}] :question/math-academy-id "q-337099" :question/problem "Consider the inexact differential equation\n$x^{2}ydx - (x^{3} + 2y^{4})dy = 0$.\nIt is known that\n$\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y} - \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}) = \\frac{4}{y}$\nwhere the functions $P$ and $Q$ are given by\n$P(x, y) = x^{2}y, Q(x, y) =-x^{3} - 2y^{4}$.\n\nUse this information to find a suitable integrating factor $I(y)$ and hence find the general solution to the equation.\n\nA suitable integrating factor is $I(y) =$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe general solution is {{field-2}}, where $c$ is a constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311864 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308782} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309237} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309483} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309237} :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311177} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}{y}^{3}+y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309513} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{y}^{3}+2y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310114} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}{y}^{3}+2y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310427} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+{x}^{3}{y}^{3}+y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}{y}^{3}+2y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310427} :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311441}] :question/math-academy-id "q-337637" :question/problem "Consider the inexact differential equation\n\n$$\n(\\frac{5{y}^{2}}{x}+2{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+(5y+2x{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\nIt is known that \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=\\frac{2}{x}\n$$\n\nwhere the functions $P$ and $Q$ are given by \n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\frac{5{y}^{2}}{x}+2{y}^{3},\\,Q(x,y)=5y+2x{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUse this information to find a suitable integrating factor $I(x)$ and hence find the general solution to the equation.$\\,$ A suitable integrating factor is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is {{field-2}}, where $c$ is a constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309535} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309851} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310310} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310718} :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/r